eeks (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Iowa's 1st District pairs Republican incumbent Mariannette Miller-Meeks with Democrat Christina Bohannan, who is challenging her for a third time in a seat that leans Republican by about four points. Every major race rating published this fall calls the seat a Democratic flip, ranging from Tilt D to Likely D, and prediction markets price Bohannan near 92 percent.\n\nBohannan has kept pace financially, raising about $9.9 million to Miller-Meeks's $9.1 million and entering the final stretch with more cash on hand, though outside groups have spent heavily against her. Direct polling is sparse: a July survey of likely voters showed her up five, and an older Democratic-sponsored poll showed a similar margin. The district's Republican lean and Miller-Meeks's incumbency remain real obstacles, but the combined weight of ratings, markets and money points to a narrow Democratic edge.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7001, "margin": 3.17}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7846, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8086, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8054, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7184, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.759, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7744, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7867, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7982, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.8113, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.8123, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.8154, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7921, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.7922, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.768, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.7631, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.8099, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.7885, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.7696, "margin": 5.0}